we want to do right.

00:10:52.210 --> 00:10:54.260
So, my dad actually taught me like

00:10:54.260 --> 00:10:56.190
how to make the perfect to-do list,

00:10:56.190 --> 00:10:57.730
which is you wake up in the morning

00:10:57.730 --> 00:10:58.910
and you think to yourself all right,

00:10:58.910 --> 00:11:00.670
you jot down everything
that you can think of

00:11:00.670 --> 00:11:03.070
that you can do, and that you have to do.

00:11:03.070 --> 00:11:06.230
You jot it down and then from that list,

00:11:06.230 --> 00:11:09.423
everything that is super
important goes to the top.

00:11:10.561 --> 00:11:13.480
Else that can wait a couple
of days goes to the bottom.

00:11:13.480 --> 00:11:15.190
And then you go on with your day,

00:11:15.190 --> 00:11:16.770
you tick off everything that you do.

00:11:16.770 --> 00:11:17.700
And at the end of the day,

00:11:17.700 --> 00:11:19.610
if you're left with a couple
of things, that's all right.

00:11:19.610 --> 00:11:23.460
That becomes the top of your
to-do list the next day.

00:11:23.460 --> 00:11:25.220
- And just, I've been doing
that for the past year

00:11:25.220 --> 00:11:27.820
