- It was very light for a ramen.

00:16:38.477 --> 00:16:39.350
- It was very light yeah.

00:16:39.350 --> 00:16:42.187
- 'Cause like when you said
like ramen, I was just like,

00:16:42.187 --> 00:16:44.007
"Oh, it's going to be a heavy ramen,"

00:16:44.007 --> 00:16:45.730
'cause ramen is the kind of meal

00:16:45.730 --> 00:16:46.970
that like takes you out.

00:16:46.970 --> 00:16:48.470
It knocks you out for like an hour

00:16:48.470 --> 00:16:49.520
because of how heavy it is.

00:16:49.520 --> 00:16:51.448
- It's like the thin
noodle ramen I guess...

00:16:51.448 --> 00:16:52.487
- It was very nice, it was good,

00:16:52.487 --> 00:16:53.910
it was light.
- It was good but...

00:16:53.910 --> 00:16:55.480
When I was thinking about it, I'm like,

00:16:55.480 --> 00:16:56.350
okay what do I...

00:16:56.350 --> 00:16:59.303
I think I have the wrong
expectations of Michelin Star.

00:16:59.303 --> 00:17:00.480
Like I expect some kind of

00:17:00.480 --> 00:17:02.407
stupid luxurious-like gourmet thing,

00:17:02.407 --> 00:17:04.801
but I guess it's more about value,

00:17:04.801 --> 00:17:06.170
the food you get.
- It was like 1000 Yen.

00:17:06.170 --> 00:17:08.030
At least the one I got was like 10 bucks.

00:17:08.030 --> 00:17:09.840
- Yeah, I mean like $8 right?

00:17:09.840 --> 00:17:10.940
- Yeah, it's amazing,

00:17:10.940 --> 00:17:12.400
I have a picture of it, I put up on...

00:17:12.400 --> 00:17:13.533
- It was very good but the
whole time I was thinking,

00:17:13.533 --> 00:17:16.020
I was like, "I think
tsukemen is more tasty there"

00:17:16.020 --> 00:17:18.720
- I think so as too.
- I think so as well.

00:17:18.720 --> 00:17:20.450
- The bulk standard tsukemen

00:17:20.450 --> 00:17:22.890
which was better than
the Michelin Star ramen.

00:17:22.890 --> 00:17:26.670
- I agree. Honestly, I didn't
enjoy the ramen that much.

00:17:26.670 --> 00:17:29.040
And I got okay, 'cause
here's the thing right?

00:17:29.040 --> 00:17:32.410
I feel like Michelin Star, if
you've been to enough of them,

00:17:32.410 --> 00:17:33.890
especially in Japan, 'cause it's like,

00:17:33.890 --> 00:17:36.590
in Japan there's so many
Michelin Star restaurants,

00:17:36.590 --> 00:17:38.560
but I've realized that,

00:17:38.560 --> 00:17:40.060
with Michelin Star, you come in with like

00:17:40.060 --> 00:17:41.810
the wrong expectations right?

00:17:41.810 --> 00:17:43.470
And this is gonna make me sound,

00:17:43.470 --> 00:17:46.108
this is gonna make me sound
so fuckin privileged and all,

00:17:46.108 --> 00:17:47.773
"Michelin Stars aren't
all that great but..."

00:17:47.773 --> 00:17:48.947
- [Connor] Where's the
Michelin Star Garnt? Tell them.

00:17:48.947 --> 00:17:50.830
- It's a Michelin Star, but like,

00:17:50.830 --> 00:17:53.330
here's the thing right.
- The Tire Man? No!

00:17:53.330 --> 00:17:55.130
(Group laughs)
- Like here's the thing.

00:17:55.130 --> 00:17:56.690
When you go into a
Michelin Star restaurant,

00:17:56.690 --> 00:17:59.030
your expectations are like
up here, you're like...

00:17:59.030 --> 00:17:59.863
- Scott knows all well

00:17:59.863 --> 00:18:01.053
because he often frequents
the Michelin Star

00:18:01.053 --> 00:18:02.360
- [Garnt] Of course, of course.

00:18:02.360 --> 00:18:05.540
No but like, you come in
with these expectations

00:18:05.540 --> 00:18:07.050
that you're gonna get like a meal

00:18:07.050 --> 00:18:09.170
that's a cut above the rest right?

00:18:09.170 --> 00:18:11.440
And so you start judging things harsher

00:18:11.440 --> 00:18:13.770
than if you just go to
this random restaurant

00:18:13.770 --> 00:18:15.400
and just like find out

00:18:15.400 --> 00:18:16.740
that there's like amazing food.

00:18:16.740 --> 00:18:18.930
'Cause in Japan, I feel like there is

00:18:18.930 --> 00:18:21.690
just as many restaurants that have food

00:18:21.690 --> 00:18:23.223
that are like Michelin Star quality,

00:18:23.223 --> 00:18:25.310
that just haven't been discovered yet?

00:18:25.310 --> 00:18:28.690
And, and to me like,

00:18:28.690 --> 00:18:31.310
Michelin Star isn't
always the indicator of,

00:18:31.310 --> 00:18:33.347
this is the best meal
that you can get in Japan.

00:18:33.347 --> 00:18:34.905
But it only means is that.

00:18:34.905 --> 00:18:36.590
It's become famous enough

00:18:36.590 --> 00:18:38.050
that people have started to notice it.

00:18:38.050 --> 00:18:40.780
But there are so many hidden gems.

00:18:40.780 --> 00:18:43.200
And like, for example, with
the Michelin Star ramen,

00:18:43.200 --> 00:18:44.600
that is not like the best,

00:18:44.600 --> 00:18:45.871
even the best ramen that I've had,

00:18:45.871 --> 00:18:46.944
the best tsukemen that I've had.

00:18:46.944 --> 00:18:49.820
- I've had like sketchy ass places

00:18:49.820 --> 00:18:51.001
that were a little bit
better. (Connor laughs)

00:18:51.001 --> 00:18:53.560
- I honestly think the insect ramen

00:18:53.560 --> 00:18:55.192
I had from my video was actually better.

00:18:55.192 --> 00:18:56.025
- No!

00:18:56.025 --> 00:18:58.225
- And that had 150 crickets in it.

00:18:58.225 --> 00:18:59.710
- I'm not shitting on this one.

00:18:59.710 --> 00:19:00.840
We haven't named the ramen place.

00:19:00.840 --> 00:19:02.390
'cause I also don't
wanna like fuckin make...

00:19:02.390 --> 00:19:03.770
- I'm saying that because the insect ramen

00:19:03.770 --> 00:19:05.400
was actually fuckin amazing.

00:19:05.400 --> 00:19:08.090
- No. And also like,
because it's Michelin Star,

00:19:08.090 --> 00:19:10.178
it actually made it a worse
experience for me right?

00:19:10.178 --> 00:19:11.397
Because you wait in line...

00:19:11.397 --> 00:19:13.750
- Because your expectations
are too high right?

00:19:13.750 --> 00:19:15.330
- One, yeah expectations is high.

00:19:15.330 --> 00:19:17.420
And two, it's really,
really fuckin busy right?

00:19:17.420 --> 00:19:20.160
So, in this ramen shop,
it's a tiny ass ramen shop.

00:19:20.160 --> 00:19:22.880
It's like, when we say
Michelin Star, it's a really...

00:19:22.880 --> 00:19:24.570
It's a normal ramen shop.

00:19:24.570 --> 00:19:27.240
- Ramen stores in general are like not...

00:19:27.240 --> 00:19:29.440
I would say they're
good dining experiences.

00:19:30.959 --> 00:19:32.730
If you wanna come here and
chill out with your friends,

00:19:32.730 --> 00:19:33.690
don't go to a ramen place.

00:19:33.690 --> 00:19:34.523
- It's a come in,

00:19:34.523 --> 00:19:35.640
eat, and go.
- Yeah, yeah.

00:19:35.640 --> 00:19:37.227
- I mean that place only seats like what?

00:19:37.227 --> 00:19:39.010
10, 12 people maybe?

00:19:39.010 --> 00:19:39.843
- [Garnt] Yeah, yeah exactly.

00:19:39.843 --> 00:19:41.300
- It's busy, it's like narrow.

00:19:41.300 --> 00:19:43.240
You're like, if you're
even remotely large,

00:19:43.240 --> 00:19:44.450
then larger than normal,

00:19:44.450 --> 00:19:47.180
you're gonna have a tough
time squeezing past everyone.

00:19:47.180 --> 00:19:48.190
It's like not fine.
- [Garnt] Unlike,

00:19:48.190 --> 00:19:49.990
We went at about 2:00 pm.

00:19:49.990 --> 00:19:51.992
So not even like, not
even close to peak time

00:19:51.992 --> 00:19:54.070
and we still had to wait
like a good 20 minutes.

00:19:54.070 --> 00:19:55.340
Like a good 20 minutes.

00:19:55.340 --> 00:19:57.300
And this is when the country
is closed to tourists,

00:19:57.300 --> 00:19:58.730
so when tourists come back in...

00:19:58.730 --> 00:20:01.220
I was talking to some people
who've waited for this ramen

00:20:01.220 --> 00:20:03.970
for like an hour, an hour
and a half, two hours right?

00:20:03.970 --> 00:20:06.140
And you get shepherd in,

00:20:06.140 --> 00:20:07.280
and then you're expected

00:20:07.280 --> 00:20:09.030
to just eat the ramen and leave right?

00:20:09.030 --> 00:20:10.300
There's no downtime.

00:20:10.300 --> 00:20:11.190
You get given a bowl,

00:20:11.190 --> 00:20:12.220
you eat it and then leave.

00:20:12.220 --> 00:20:14.800
You can't like, to me, part
of like the food experience,

00:20:14.800 --> 00:20:18.270
is just like, not feeling
pressured to eat the food,

00:20:18.270 --> 00:20:19.230
but just...
- [Joey] Yeah.

00:20:19.230 --> 00:20:20.500
- But just like, feeling like,

00:20:20.500 --> 00:20:22.715
I can take my time to enjoy this food.

00:20:22.715 --> 00:20:24.190
- I couldn't even like bask.

00:20:24.190 --> 00:20:25.770
Like as good as the ramen was,

00:20:25.770 --> 00:20:27.387
I couldn't bask in it because

00:20:27.387 --> 00:20:29.490
there was the pressure of all.

00:20:29.490 --> 00:20:30.680
I could take my time with this,

00:20:30.680 --> 00:20:32.700
but I'd also be pissing
off the 20 other people

00:20:32.700 --> 00:20:33.620
still waiting in line right?

00:20:33.620 --> 00:20:34.620
- [Garnt] Exactly right, exactly.

00:20:34.620 --> 00:20:35.453
- Standing outside.

00:20:35.453 --> 00:20:36.920
- This is why I've realized

00:20:36.920 --> 00:20:40.340
that ramen is best at like midnight.

00:20:40.340 --> 00:20:41.610
- You can just like...

00:20:41.610 --> 00:20:42.470
- They take their time with it.

00:20:42.470 --> 00:20:43.500
- They always serve beers.

00:20:43.500 --> 00:20:44.893
Everyone's having like
a good time in there,

00:20:44.893 --> 00:20:46.740
like it's a way more fun atmosphere.

00:20:46.740 --> 00:20:48.180
Like some of the stores
that are open 24 hours

00:20:48.180 --> 00:20:50.220
normally have a few more seats as well.

00:20:50.220 --> 00:20:53.150
- It is the ultimate
midnight snack for sure.

00:20:53.150 --> 00:20:54.508
- Honestly it's awful for your stomach.

00:20:54.508 --> 00:20:55.341
(Joey chuckles)

00:20:55.341 --> 00:20:57.464
There's a good chance you
might like bring it back up.

00:20:57.464 --> 00:21:00.387
But some of the best
ramen experiences I've had

00:21:00.387 --> 00:21:01.470
are like midnight.

00:21:01.470 --> 00:21:02.720
We're in like a sketchy area

00:21:02.720 --> 00:21:04.920
of some place in Japan.

00:21:04.920 --> 00:21:06.660
Everyone's drinking beers in the store,

00:21:06.660 --> 00:21:08.340
it's cool atmosphere, everyone's talking.

00:21:08.340 --> 00:21:10.270
It's so much more fun
than ramen during the day

00:21:10.270 --> 00:21:12.070
where everyone's just
there to eat and get out.

00:21:12.070 --> 00:21:13.940
- Yeah, the best ramen experience I had

00:21:13.940 --> 00:21:15.595
was when I was absolutely shit faced,

00:21:15.595 --> 00:21:16.784
(Connor and Garnt laughing)

00:21:16.784 --> 00:21:17.850
at like 2:00 am.

00:21:17.850 --> 00:21:19.616
And then my friend Makoto was like,

00:21:19.616 --> 00:21:20.990
(Joey speaking Japanese)

00:21:20.990 --> 00:21:23.470
at like 2:00 am and I was like, uh okay.

00:21:23.470 --> 00:21:24.410
So, we ran around the corner

00:21:24.410 --> 00:21:26.470
to this like awful sketchy place.

00:21:26.470 --> 00:21:28.227
Like the ramen wasn't even
that good bu just like...

00:21:28.227 --> 00:21:29.480
- It's just fun.

00:21:29.480 --> 00:21:30.570
- It's just fun.

00:21:30.570 --> 00:21:33.030
When the moment I went
down, I was like damn!

00:21:33.030 --> 00:21:33.863
Good to feel alive.

00:21:33.863 --> 00:21:35.420
But then the moment you
walk out it's like...

00:21:35.420 --> 00:21:36.630
- Oh it's awful.

00:21:36.630 --> 00:21:37.610
- 'Cause you've ruined your stomach

00:21:37.610 --> 00:21:39.107
with all the alcohol.
- Be right back in the diner.

00:21:39.107 --> 00:21:41.170
- 'Cause to me like the
restaurant experience

00:21:41.170 --> 00:21:43.920
goes beyond just the
taste of the food right?

00:21:43.920 --> 00:21:46.140
There's like a reason
why your mom's cooking

00:21:46.140 --> 00:21:47.690
always tastes fuckin good right?

00:21:47.690 --> 00:21:48.570
It's 'cause like...

00:21:48.570 --> 00:21:51.317
'Cause that cooking mean
something to you (stutters).

00:21:51.317 --> 00:21:53.956
- "Where's the heart man?
Where's the heart in the ramen?"

00:21:53.956 --> 00:21:55.800
(Connor laughs)
- Honestly, honestly!

00:21:55.800 --> 00:21:57.780
you can taste in some Japanese restaurants

00:21:57.780 --> 00:21:59.540
where they put the heart to the cooking.

00:21:59.540 --> 00:22:00.373
- [Joey] Oh yeah, yeah.

00:22:00.373 --> 00:22:03.970
- Like it's so obvious with
some like very small shops.

00:22:03.970 --> 00:22:06.530
- I mean I just think that I just,

00:22:06.530 --> 00:22:08.280
I realized that I don't like ramen

00:22:08.280 --> 00:22:10.458
as much as I want to like ramen.

00:22:10.458 --> 00:22:14.100
Like I Uber Eats tsukemen on sometimes.

00:22:14.100 --> 00:22:15.757
And that shit is fuckin good.

00:22:15.757 --> 00:22:18.160
Because also ramen travels terribly.

00:22:18.160 --> 00:22:20.260
That's why I never, ever order ramen.

00:22:20.260 --> 00:22:21.490
I mean unless you have like one of those

00:22:21.490 --> 00:22:22.323
really old style ones,

00:22:22.323 --> 00:22:24.210
where they like, bring you actual bowl

00:22:24.210 --> 00:22:25.043
with everything in it.

00:22:25.043 --> 00:22:25.876
- That's the only one I get.

00:22:25.876 --> 00:22:27.700
- Problem is nowadays with
ramen, with Uber Eats.

00:22:27.700 --> 00:22:29.370
They separate the noodles and the broth.

00:22:29.370 --> 00:22:30.880
So they just give you a broth
in like a plastic thing.

00:22:30.880 --> 00:22:32.270
- Really?
- A lot of the time yeah.

00:22:32.270 --> 00:22:33.520
They don't actually put the noodles in.

00:22:33.520 --> 00:22:35.150
You have to put the noodles in yourself.

00:22:35.150 --> 00:22:35.983
Yeah it's not good.

00:22:35.983 --> 00:22:36.940
And the noodles are supposed to be

00:22:36.940 --> 00:22:38.800
like piping hot in the broth.

00:22:38.800 --> 00:22:39.723
So, it doesn't really work.

00:22:39.723 --> 00:22:43.370
But tsukemen, it travels
pretty okay, 'cause you...

00:22:43.370 --> 00:22:46.022
- It's because the broth is
so thick, it's like magma.

00:22:46.022 --> 00:22:47.102
It stays hot forever.
- The Broth is so thick

00:22:47.102 --> 00:22:47.991
It stays really hot,

00:22:47.991 --> 00:22:49.317
and then the noodles are
supposed to be separate anyway.

00:22:49.317 --> 00:22:51.177
And then you just dunk the noodles in

00:22:51.177 --> 00:22:53.740
and it's almost as good as you get it.

00:22:53.740 --> 00:22:55.580
- Definitely better than shop at but yeah.

00:22:55.580 --> 00:22:59.350
- But like if you need that itch.

00:22:59.350 --> 00:23:00.190
- So, I've been saying man.

00:23:00.190 --> 00:23:01.050
I've been advocating for.

00:23:01.050 --> 00:23:03.570
- Because like ramen is
that one Japanese dish

00:23:03.570 --> 00:23:05.290
where before I moved to Japan,

00:23:05.290 --> 00:23:06.123
I was thinking oh,

00:23:06.123 --> 00:23:08.407
I'm gonna eat ramen every
fuckin week, every day.

00:23:08.407 --> 00:23:09.790
- I realize I've had ramen

00:23:09.790 --> 00:23:12.060
three times in the past week. (chuckles)

00:23:12.060 --> 00:23:14.230
But I didn't have ramen for
like months before that.

00:23:14.230 --> 00:23:15.823
- Yeah, I was saying like the last time

00:23:15.823 --> 00:23:17.260
I had ramen before we went to this

00:23:17.260 --> 00:23:19.130
Michelin Star ramen place,

00:23:19.130 --> 00:23:20.914
was like I think...

00:23:20.914 --> 00:23:21.747
- A year before.

00:23:21.747 --> 00:23:22.750
- A year before.

00:23:22.750 --> 00:23:23.710
That's just because I have like

00:23:23.710 --> 00:23:24.950
zero craving for ramen.

00:23:24.950 --> 00:23:25.890
'Cause why would I have ramen

00:23:25.890 --> 00:23:27.820
when I can have tsukemen right?

00:23:27.820 --> 00:23:29.000
Like but the one dish that

00:23:29.000 --> 00:23:31.170
I haven't got bored off though is sushi.

00:23:31.170 --> 00:23:33.290
Like I eat sushi at least once a week.

00:23:33.290 --> 00:23:34.123
- Really?

00:23:34.123 --> 00:23:34.956
- At least once a week.

00:23:34.956 --> 00:23:35.940
(Garnt laughs)
- You eat it more than me,

00:23:35.940 --> 00:23:36.870
And I love sushi.

00:23:36.870 --> 00:23:39.500
I'd probably go maybe like
two or three times a month.

00:23:39.500 --> 00:23:41.390
- I wish there was like a really

00:23:41.390 --> 00:23:42.840
quick and easy one near my house.

00:23:42.840 --> 00:23:43.673
I would probably go.

00:23:43.673 --> 00:23:45.070
I don't wanna order it.

00:23:45.070 --> 00:23:46.537
- Yeah no, it doesn't order well.

00:23:46.537 --> 00:23:48.920
But like, I feel like there's a few

00:23:48.920 --> 00:23:50.330
conveyor belts sushis near my place,

00:23:50.330 --> 00:23:52.230
and it's just perfect for lunch man.

00:23:52.230 --> 00:23:54.237
It's quick, it's easy.
- They're like 100 Yen,

00:23:54.237 --> 00:23:55.680
'cause even like the 100 Yen sushi,

00:23:55.680 --> 00:23:57.320
which is like 80 cents

00:23:57.320 --> 00:23:59.610
for like one piece of
like salmon or something.

00:23:59.610 --> 00:24:00.800
It's so good.

00:24:00.800 --> 00:24:02.250
- Yeah, honestly like my experience

00:24:02.250 --> 00:24:05.870
with sushi in Japan is that, I've also...

00:24:05.870 --> 00:24:06.703
Maylin has taken me

00:24:06.703 --> 00:24:08.710
to some Michelin Star sushi places as well

00:24:08.710 --> 00:24:09.543
- But of course she has.

00:24:09.543 --> 00:24:11.254
- Maylin only eats if there's

00:24:11.254 --> 00:24:12.376
(Garnt laughs)
Michelin man inside.

00:24:12.376 --> 00:24:14.237
She's like, "I don't see
the Michelin man anywhere,

00:24:14.237 --> 00:24:15.230
"I'm not going in."

00:24:15.230 --> 00:24:16.810
- Basically part of the big reason

00:24:16.810 --> 00:24:18.800
why we've gone to more
Michelin Star places

00:24:18.800 --> 00:24:20.770
is because Maylin suggested

00:24:20.770 --> 00:24:22.480
these places to us.
- Maylin swears by it.

00:24:22.480 --> 00:24:24.920
- Yeah, which is how we
found the ramen place.

00:24:24.920 --> 00:24:26.517
which is Maylin
recommended the ramen place

00:24:26.517 --> 00:24:28.440
and it happens to be Michelin Star.

00:24:28.440 --> 00:24:31.910
But I have tried like, a few like,

00:24:31.910 --> 00:24:33.570
a lot of different sushi places

00:24:33.570 --> 00:24:34.920
of like different price points.

00:24:34.920 --> 00:24:39.061
And my honest opinion is that like sushi,

00:24:39.061 --> 00:24:40.719
you reach about like,

00:24:40.719 --> 00:24:43.080
you reached about like
$30 a meal for a sushi,

00:24:43.080 --> 00:24:46.730
which is about, mid range
sushi in Japan right?

00:24:46.730 --> 00:24:48.280
It's not cheap, it's not expensive.

00:24:48.280 --> 00:24:51.450
And that's about as good as it gets to me,

00:24:51.450 --> 00:24:53.890
because you can get sushi

00:24:53.890 --> 00:24:56.140
from like $30, like $100, like $200.

